<title>CHINA: China's Ningbo cargo handling ranks third largest.</title>
<headline>China's Ningbo cargo handling ranks third largest.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ningbo port in eastern China's Zhejiang province handled 76.3 million tonnes of cargo in 1996, the Economic Information Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ningbo had become the third largest Chinese port in terms of cargo handling, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Qinhuangdao in the northern province of Hebei was second while Shanghai was first, it said. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
